---
layout: article
title: Zero
description: Use the Appwrite CLI to start and manage Appwrite Zero projects without an account.
---

Running `zero` creates an [Appwrite Zero](/docs/zero) project without an account and links it to the current directory. Additional `zero` subcommands report remaining time, open the Console, extend the build window, list Zero projects created on this machine, and delete a project.

{% info title="CLI version" %}
`appwrite zero` requires Appwrite CLI 28.15.0 or later. [Update the CLI](/docs/tooling/command-line/installation#update-your-cli) to the latest release first.
{% /info %}

# Start a Zero project {% #create %}

Run `zero` inside an existing app directory, or pass a directory name to create a new one:

```sh
appwrite zero
appwrite zero my-app
```

The CLI writes `appwrite.config.json`, signs in to the new project, and prints the project ID, endpoint, and claim link. Follow-up commands such as `appwrite push` run against that project right away.

{% info title="Active session" %}
Creating a Zero project switches the CLI's active session to that project. To return to your own account, run `appwrite login --switch`.
{% /info %}

# Check project status {% #status %}

```sh
appwrite zero status
```

```text
projectId     : <PROJECT_ID>
status        : active
endpoint      : https://fra.cloud.appwrite.io/v1
buildTimeLeft : 49m
claimTimeLeft : 1d 49m
claimUrl      : https://appwrite.io/transfer?transferId=<TRANSFER_ID>&secret=<SECRET>
expiresAt     : 2026-11-25 08:02:16 UTC (in 49m)
claimBy       : 2026-11-26 08:02:16 UTC (in 1d)

ownerLinks
  https://<DOMAIN>.appwrite.network/__appwrite/zero?token=<TOKEN>
```

The `ownerLinks` section provides one URL per site and function domain. Open any of these links in a browser to view private deployment previews for that domain.

# Available commands {% #commands %}

```sh
appwrite zero [directory] [options]
appwrite zero [command] [options]
```

{% table %}
* Command
* Description
---
* `zero [directory]`
* Create a Zero project and link it to the given directory, defaulting to the current directory when omitted.
---
* `zero status`
* Display the remaining build and claim times, the claim link, and the owner links for each project domain.
---
* `zero console`
* Open the project in the Console under its temporary owner account using a single-use link valid for a few minutes.
---
* `zero extend`
* Add one hour to the build window and resume a paused project. Allowed up to three times, and never past the claim deadline.
---
* `zero list`
* List all Zero projects created on this machine along with each project's remaining time and claim link.
---
* `zero delete`
* Remove the project ahead of the claim deadline. Requires confirmation unless `--force` is passed.
{% /table %}

# Command options {% #options %}

{% table %}
* Option
* Description
---
* `--region <region>`
* Place the new project in `fra`, `nyc`, `sfo`, `sgp`, `syd`, or `tor`. Defaults to the nearest region.
---
* `--json`
* Output results as JSON. With `zero`, includes the claim link and the access token for private previews. With `zero console`, prints the sign-in link without launching a browser.
---
* `--force`
* Bypass the confirmation prompt on `zero delete` when running from agents or scripts.
{% /table %}
